# Build context filter. Everything matched here is excluded from the context
# tarball that Docker sends to the daemon, and therefore from any COPY source.
#
# The load-bearing line is `**/node_modules`. Without it, BuildKit tries to
# hash every file inside apps/api/node_modules during `COPY apps/api ./apps/api`.
# That directory contains npm workspace symlinks (e.g. @ticketing/shared →
# ../../packages/shared), and if any link in the tree is broken, the hash
# computation aborts with the misleading error
#   failed to compute cache key: ".../apps/api": not found
# The directory does exist; the file-walk failed.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image by the deps stage
**/node_modules

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Env files — never bake secrets into images
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local dev artifacts
**/.pgdata
**/.cert
*.log
coverage

# Git history — irrelevant for build, and .git can hold refs BuildKit cannot
# resolve cleanly (partial clones, gc)
.git
.gitignore

# Editors
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# Docs and screenshots
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Test artifacts
apps/api/test-results
